420: This completes the actual page-line comparison.
421: 
422: ## K28.5. The signed trace and the characteristic calculation
423: 
424: Near the single point at infinity of (K28.13), write
425: \(\xi\sim c w^{-m_0}\), \(\eta\sim d w^{-m_\infty}\).
426: The complex boundary of the punctured page has parameter
427: \(-\arg w=\beta\). By (K28.12), the positive physical parameter
428: is exactly \(\theta=\beta\). Hence
429: \(\partial V=+E\times S^1_\theta\).
430: Orient the actual nodal compression by \(\partial W=F-E\).
431: Its rotated product attaches to give a trace with
432: \(\partial X=+F\times S^1_\theta\).
433: 
434: In the actual Hopf chart the ambient orientation is
435: \(\operatorname{or}(F)\operatorname{or}(\nu_{\rm Hopf})\,dr\,d\theta\),
436: whereas the trace orientation is
437: \(\operatorname{or}(F)\,dr\,d\theta\).
438: Moving the three normal directions past the last two is even.
439: The induced normal sphere is therefore the positive Hopf sphere
440: and its actual Euler line satisfies \(\pi_*x=+1\).
441: This is the full signed Thom comparison, for both
442: \(\varepsilon=1\) and \(\varepsilon=-1\). Any source-product
443: orientation reversal in the three-sphere map is already included
444: in this normal comparison and introduces no additional sign.
445: 
446: The two outer-boundary/Jin reversals are the ones proved in
447: P3K.7. Its actual trace bordism, with the page-line map just
448: constructed, gives
449: \[
450:             A^{\rm Jin}
451:               =\frac{12\,c_1(N)^2-p_1(TS_{\rm page})}{24}.
452:  \tag{K28.27}
453: \]
454: The compression cap and the regular elliptic cap have the exact
455: boundary line comparison of P3K.5--7, zero signature, and zero
456: line-square ambiguity. Thus the right side may be computed on
457: the compact sectioned elliptic page. This uses the displayed
458: relative maps, not a holomorphic compactification of the original
459: parameter family.
460: 
461: Let the original capped Euler numbers be \(e_\infty,e_0\),
462: and the actual minimal root Euler numbers be
463: \(e_\infty',e_0'\). There are \(m_0\) copies of the first root
464: and \(m_\infty\) of the second. Every other fibre is unramified.
465: Consequently
466: \[
467:  \chi(\mathcal O_{S_{\rm page}})
468:    =\frac{M(12-e_\infty-e_0)
469:             +m_0e_\infty'+m_\infty e_0'}{12}.
470:  \tag{K28.28}
471: \]
472: Its signature is \(-8\chi\) and its tangent Pontryagin number is
473: \(-24\chi\). The actual marked line section \(aG'\) meets the
474: identity component at every remaining reducible fibre and at
475: each reduced root in the listed cases; good roots are irreducible.
476: The height base-change formula, with \(h(G)=1/d\), gives
477: \[
478:  h(aG')=\frac{Ma^2}{d}
479:        =2\chi+2(P_{aG'}\cdot O),\qquad
480:  c_1(N)^2=-\frac{Ma^2}{d}.
481:  \tag{K28.29}
482: \]
483: For the quadratic starred line this formula uses \(N\) from
484: (K28.21), so no root correction from \(-L_0\) is omitted.
485: Combining the actual comparison with (K28.27) yields
486: \[
487:                     A^{\rm Jin}
488:                          =\chi-\frac{Ma^2}{2d}
489:                          =-P_{aG'}\cdot O .
490:  \tag{K28.30}
491: \]
492: 
493: ## K28.6. All joint return values and the one-star specialization
494: 
495: The following tables are evaluated only on the sphere tuples
496: \(D=\pm1\), with the exact signed parameter (K28.2). For each
497: fixed row and fixed root orders, both determinant signs give
498: the displayed integer. The actual proof of this equality of
499: signs is (K28.4)--(K28.27).
500: 
501: For the E6 source of F46, \(d=6\), the other source fibre is
502: the selected \(I_1\), and the values are:
503: 
504: | \((a,b)\) | \(m_\infty\) at \(IV^*\) | \(m_0\) at III | Actual \(A^{\rm Jin}\) |
505: |---|---|---|---|
506: | \((1,6)\) | \(3l\), good | \(4k\), good | \(0\) |
507: | \((2,3)\) | \(3l\), good | \(4k+1\), reduced III | \(-3lk\) |
508: | \((3,2)\) | \(3l+2\), reduced IV | \(4k\), good | \(-4k(2l+1)\) |
509: | \((6,1)\) | \(3l+2\), reduced IV | \(4k+1\), reduced III | \(-35lk-8l-22k-5\) |
510: 
511: The good-root indices are positive and the reduced-root indices
512: are nonnegative. The unit determinant also retains every
513: coprimality restriction; for example the third row requires
514: \(3l+2\) odd. These restrictions are not removed from the table.
515: 
516: For the E7 source of F47, \(d=2\), the other source fibre is again
517: the selected \(I_1\):
518: 
519: | \((a,b)\) | \(m_\infty\) at \(III^*\) | \(m_0\) at II | Actual \(A^{\rm Jin}\) |
520: |---|---|---|---|
521: | \((2,1)\) | \(4l+3\), reduced III | \(6k+1\), reduced II | \(-22lk-3l-15k-2\) |
522: | \((2,1)\) | \(4l+3\), reduced III | \(6k\), good | \(-k(22l+15)\) |
523: | \((1,2)\) | \(4l\), good | \(6k+1\), reduced II | \(-4lk\) |
524: 
525: The fourth formal root combination, good \(III^*\) and good II,
